  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_003 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. All scvi_n200 multimodal models substantially outperform scgpt-based ones, and within scvi_n200, transformer aggregation + weighted fusion + imagenet_vit_l is the top combination. However, we have only tested weighted fusion with scvi_n200; the scgpt experiments (config_001 vs config_004) showed only a marginal weighted-over-concat advantage (~1.3% acc). Question: config_046 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) isolates the fusion method as the sole variable relative to the current best, testing whether weighted fusion provides a genuine contribution in the high-performing scvi_n200 regime or whether concat is sufficient. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable A/B comparison against the incumbent best, directly reducing uncertainty about a core design choice (fusion) without introducing confounds. If concat matches weighted, the design space simplifies; if weighted is clearly superior, we confirm the current best is well-chosen. Under a limited budget, exploiting the strongest evidence while isolating one remaining uncertainty is more efficient than jumping to a less-explored axis (e.g., singleprofile) that would change multiple variables simultaneously."
}

